      "message": "The matrix `R` defined here is mathematically a **+90 degree** rotation matrix (assuming standard column vectors). However, because `rotate()` multiplies the vector as a row vector (`v^T * R`), it effectively applies the transpose of the matrix, resulting in a **-90 degree** rotation. This is why the expected rotated vector on line 85 has `-10` for the Y axis instead of `10`.\\n\\nYou might want to update this comment to clarify this behavior, e.g., `/* +90 degree rotation matrix (results in -90 deg rotation due to row-vector multiplication in rotate()) */` to prevent any confusion for future readers.",
